WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.620
A field gives a harvest.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.480
But who pays the tax on it?

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.480
Company rule in India tried

4
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.730
three answers.

5
00:00:09.365 --> 00:00:11.165
Bengal: fixed forever.

6
00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:13.045
The Permanent Settlement,

7
00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:15.305
seventeen ninety three.

8
00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:17.525
Rajas and taluqdars became

9
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:19.505
zamindars, and paid a revenue

10
00:00:19.505 --> 00:00:21.095
fixed for all time.

11
00:00:21.625 --> 00:00:23.285
Pay by sunset.

12
00:00:23.285 --> 00:00:25.605
Miss sunset on the due date, and

13
00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:27.585
the estate could be auctioned.

14
00:00:27.585 --> 00:00:30.125
Three in four zamindaris changed

15
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:30.995
hands.

16
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:32.950
The auction that wasn't.

17
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.130
Burdwan, seventeen ninety seven.

18
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.950
The raja's estates were

19
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.870
auctioned, mostly to his own

20
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.390
servants and agents.

21
00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.610
He sold his lands, largely to

22
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.460
himself.

23
00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:45.890
The north:

24
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.370
the village pays.

25
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.770
Mahalwari, eighteen twenty two,

26
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.010
devised by Holt Mackenzie.

27
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.370
Revenue fixed for each village,

28
00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.290
revised from time to time,

29
00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.960
collected by the headman.

30
00:00:58.478 --> 00:00:59.458
The south:

31
00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:00.798
the peasant pays.

32
00:01:00.798 --> 00:01:03.798
Ryotwari, tried by Alexander

33
00:01:03.798 --> 00:01:05.738
Read and developed by Thomas

34
00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:08.158
Munro. Settled directly with the

35
00:01:08.158 --> 00:01:10.548
cultivator, field by field.

36
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.910
Who lost?

37
00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.410
In the Deccan, demands were so

38
00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:16.470
high that peasants left their

39
00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.060
villages, or borrowed to pay.

40
00:01:20.223 --> 00:01:20.803
For GS1.

41
00:01:20.803 --> 00:01:22.343
Permanent Settlement, with

42
00:01:22.343 --> 00:01:23.543
zamindars, fixed.

43
00:01:23.543 --> 00:01:26.883
Mahalwari, with the village.

44
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:29.123
Ryotwari, with the ryot.

45
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:31.413
The last two were revised.

46
00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:35.107
Three systems, one field.

47
00:01:35.107 --> 00:01:37.907
And the same farmer, bent over

48
00:01:37.907 --> 00:01:38.707
it.
